  "responseTimeMs": 17471,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return of an individual is on or before April 15 of the following year after the close of the taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor individuals, this deadline is crucial for compliance with tax obligations. Failing to file on time may result in penalties and interest on any taxes owed. Taxpayers should ensure that they prepare their returns in advance to meet this deadline and avoid any potential issues with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
